# What never goes into an image.
#
# The one that matters is `.env`: a build context is copied into the image, and an image is
# pushed to a registry and left lying around. The container gets its secrets from the
# environment at run time (see infra/docker-compose.prod.yml), never from the build.
#
# Everything else here is either rebuilt inside the image (node_modules, dist, .next) or is not
# needed to run it (docs, the design file, agent tooling, local logs).

# --- secrets and local state ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
logs/
*.log

# --- rebuilt inside the image ---
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
.next/
**/.next/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/
drizzle/

# --- not part of the app ---
.git/
.gitignore
docs/
duke.pen
_bmad/
.claude/
.agents/
.vscode/
.idea/
README.md
